# c

> A short-named public repo. This wrap points back to the source files.

## Purpose
Give a plain-language door to fitzyracing1/c so the one-letter name is not a dead end.

## How it works (plain English)
1. Keep the original repo as the place for files.
2. Use this clone only to explain the idea.
3. Send the reader back to the source for any run.

## Key ideas
- Short name (the repo is just c)
- Wrap (this page explains; it does not replace)

## The actual code
```
# source: fitzyracing1/c
open_source()
```

## Line-by-line translation
1. open_source() → “go to fitzyracing1/c for the files”

## Decisions the program makes
- If a reader needs the files → send them to the source
- If a reader needs the idea → stay on this listing

## What a person would notice
A named wrap on a one-letter door.

## Current status
Barrage clone.

## Next possible steps
Open fitzyracing1/c.
